WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.620
When our next guest got diagnosed with COVID-19,

2
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.730
he said the doctors and nurses not only saved his life,

3
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.240
but ultimately became his guardian angels.

4
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.853
Please take a look at his story.

5
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.630 line:15%
Hi, my name's Kevin Devine.

6
00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:18.710 line:15%
I'm from Staten Island, New York.

7
00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:23.050 line:15%
I came down with COVID on March 28, 2020.

8
00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:25.550
They were pumping me with all different drugs at the time

9
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.300
they thought were going to work and I was getting worse.

10
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.470
My oxygen level was down to almost six,

11
00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.040
it's clear and simple, I was dying.

12
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.410
The doctor came in, he says, Kevin,

13
00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.040
I got to put you on a ventilator.

14
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.240
I said to him, doc, I'm not going on a ventilator.

15
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.960
Everybody's gone on a ventilator has died or is dying.

16
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.590
So at the time I didn't know her name,

17
00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:46.010
but her name is Janine,

18
00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.630
young nurse I had two nights in a row.

19
00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:50.560
She sits down next to me at the edge of the bed and goes,

20
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:51.953
you remind me of my dad.

21
00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.980
And if my father was sitting in that bed right now,

22
00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:58.870
I would tell my father to go on that ventilator.

23
00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.123
The next thing I know,

24
00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.690
I woke up 42 days later,

25
00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.610
the nurse in the room jumped to the sky.

26
00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.810
She goes, oh my God, you're alive!

27
00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.180
'Cause I was just laying there like in a coma.

28
00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.920
I had to learn how to walk, had to learn how to talk,

29
00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:16.600
had to learn how to feed myself.

30
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.820
I lost 105 pounds.

31
00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:19.860
There's no family.

32
00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.690
My son, my daughter, my wife couldn't come.

33
00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:26.370
So my nurses, they were my angels, they, you know,

34
00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:31.370
gave me that, hey, you're gonna do it, you're gonna do it.

35
00:01:33.032 --> 00:01:34.400
You got to do it.

36
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.650
And one nurse, I never got her name,

37
00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.193
I'm so sorry I didn't,

38
00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.340
came in the room one night, I was having a bad night.

39
00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:45.060
I thank this nurse to this day,

40
00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.160
she called my wife and said, hey, can you send a picture?

41
00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.660
So they downloaded it and they printed it up

42
00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:51.950
and the girl brought it in the room.

43
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:53.610
She goes, hey, maybe this will help.

44
00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:57.680
And I stared at that picture day and night,

45
00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.730
that was my will to get home,

46
00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:03.510
my will to get strong, my will to keep fighting.

47
00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:07.530
I really wish if she's out there and she sees this,

48
00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:10.140
that I can one day get together with her

49
00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:12.560
to tell her how that little gesture from her

50
00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:13.883
meant so much to me.

51
00:02:15.363 --> 00:02:17.946
(crowd cheers)

52
00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.361
Hi Drew.

53
00:02:20.361 --> 00:02:21.194
Hi Kevin.

54
00:02:21.194 --> 00:02:22.646
How are you?

55
00:02:22.646 --> 00:02:25.857
I am just, I'm so moved by your story.

56
00:02:25.857 --> 00:02:26.920
Thank you, thank you for having me.

57
00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:31.590
I'm so compelled by so many aspects of your story.

58
00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:33.840
How does it feel for you,

59
00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.750
retelling it now that there has been some time,

60
00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.990
but putting yourself back in these moments?

61
00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.120
It's tough Drew, like watching the video,

62
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.870
you can see it, my eyes started to well up.

63
00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:45.800
Mine too, yeah absolutely.

64
00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.410
That's unfair 'cause I pride myself

65
00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:48.690 line:15%
on being this big, tough guy.

66
00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:50.830 line:15%
And here I am, very first time I get on TV

67
00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.190 line:15%
and I got tears in my eyes.

68
00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.150 line:15%
So, kind of came off like, oh my God,

69
00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.070 line:15%
I gotta get my composure here.

70
00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.760
And like I said in the story, the young nurse, Janine,

71
00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.350
sat at the edge of the bed with me and told me,

72
00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:01.183
go on the ventilator.

73
00:03:01.183 --> 00:03:02.361
You gotta remember Drew,

74
00:03:02.361 --> 00:03:03.690
I'm watching TV and everybody on the ventilators,

75
00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:04.940
they're dying.

76
00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:06.460
And I don't want to be,

77
00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.740
I don't want to say this and sound rude or anything,

78
00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.280
but there was a truck outside

79
00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.920
filled with bodies of people who didn't make it.

80
00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.690
That's how fast people were dying.

81
00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:17.270
So now this young nurse, Janine, I love her.

82
00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.670
I can say, she's, I'm gonna say this line

83
00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.090
and I hope you understand what I'm saying.

84
00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.580
She, those three girls are my Charlie's Angels,

85
00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:24.613
they really were.

86
00:03:26.845 --> 00:03:28.088
I love that so much.
(crowd applauds)

87
00:03:28.088 --> 00:03:31.588
They mean more than my Charlie's Angels.

88
00:03:32.877 --> 00:03:34.810
You know, and then when I made the decision,

89
00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:38.480
I'm in the room and nurses on the right, nurses on the left,

90
00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:41.080
they're putting all these things on me, getting me ready.

91
00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:44.680
And this one nurse, Tina Marie, I grabbed her hand.

92
00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:46.650
I says, listen, don't let me die.

93
00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:47.680
Don't let me die.

94
00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.330
And I looked at her and I says, if I die,

95
00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.410
you please let them know I love them.

96
00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:53.660
You let my wife and my kids know I love them.

97
00:03:54.637 --> 00:03:56.070
I may not ever see them.

98
00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.850
So, you're going through that

99
00:03:58.829 --> 00:04:00.870
and while you're going through all that,

100
00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.190
you know, next thing you know,

101
00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.580
the doctor's wheeling you in.

102
00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:04.530
And he's telling the guy,

103
00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.753
the anesthesiologist start hitting, you know,

104
00:04:07.877 --> 00:04:09.300
so the guy, the anesthesiologist looks at him and goes, why?

105
00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.070
He goes, I'm crying.

106
00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:12.380
The doctor even said, I'm crying.

107
00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:15.850
This guy's, the emotion coming through him.

108
00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:19.543
And like I said, then I woke up, like I said, 42 days later.

109
00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:22.960
I opened my eyes and the nurse in the room had her tray

110
00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:24.530
and she throws the tray in the air

111
00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.910
'cause she's scared out of her mind.

112
00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.610
She looks down at me, she goes, oh my God, he's alive.

113
00:04:29.645 --> 00:04:30.850
And you know when somebody says that to you,

114
00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:33.350
and you're looking around like, yeah I'm alive.

115
00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:34.183
Of course I'm alive.

116
00:04:34.183 --> 00:04:35.560
I'm not supposed to be dead, am I?

117
00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.000
Should I, you know, like, you know...

118
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.647
Where was I, where am I?

119
00:04:38.647 --> 00:04:40.470
And you gotta remember I got a tube in my mouth,

120
00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:41.664
I got a thing in my throat.

121
00:04:41.664 --> 00:04:42.497
(imitating struggling to talk)

122
00:04:42.497 --> 00:04:45.063
You know, trying to say I'm alive, I'm alive.

123
00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:48.670
And then that nurse in that hospital,

124
00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.970
and I never got in touch with her yet.

125
00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:54.210
I hope that somehow she's watching, if you are,

126
00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.630
you remember this story, you have to,

127
00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.310
'cause I'll never forget it.

128
00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.760
She came in the room and I was having a real bad day

129
00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.723
and I was getting upset and she said,

130
00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.060
let me see what I can do for you.

131
00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:06.450
And she just took this upon herself.

132
00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:07.740
She reached out to my wife, Laurie,

133
00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.320
got in touch with Laurie.

134
00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:10.290
And the next thing you know,

135
00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.470
she come in the room and she showed me that picture

136
00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:13.820
that you saw on the screen.

137
00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:15.920
And you know, of course you cry.

138
00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:16.753
'Cause...

139
00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.123
(choked up) Family.

140
00:05:20.018 --> 00:05:22.730
Yes, I understand. (crying)
It's all you got.

141
00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:27.380
And, I said, that was total motivation,

142
00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:30.240
total motivation and Drew, I can't thank her enough.

143
00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:32.140
I can't thank her enough because

144
00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.490
I don't know if I would've made it.

145
00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:37.080
You know, it's easy to quit in life.

146
00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:37.920
Thank God for her.

147
00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.354
Have you gotten to speak with her?

148
00:05:39.354 --> 00:05:40.520
No, I have not gotten to speak to her.

149
00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.680
That's why I hope in one way or another,

150
00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:45.650
somebody gets this to her and I would love,

151
00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:49.000
love to get together with her one time.

152
00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.660
Well, I have someone else here

153
00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.070
that I want to surprise you with.

154
00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:53.170
Oh no, no you're not.

155
00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:54.630
I am.

156
00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:57.810
It's actually the doctor that you spoke of,

157
00:05:57.810 --> 00:06:01.150
Dr. Victoria Twito, if you don't mind coming out, please.

158
00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:02.316
Thank you.

159
00:06:02.316 --> 00:06:05.192
(crowd cheers)

160
00:06:05.192 --> 00:06:06.025
How are you?

161
00:06:06.025 --> 00:06:07.351
I'm good, you look amazing.

162
00:06:07.351 --> 00:06:08.340
Thank you.

163
00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:10.483
(inaudible talk)

164
00:06:10.483 --> 00:06:12.866
That's the picture, those are the girls.

165
00:06:12.866 --> 00:06:14.032
Hi.
That's Laurie.

166
00:06:14.032 --> 00:06:15.714
That's Laurie and Michelle.

167
00:06:15.714 --> 00:06:16.547
Sit down, sit down, come on.

168
00:06:16.547 --> 00:06:17.380
I have to catch up with you.

169
00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:18.590
Oh my gosh.

170
00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:19.740
I have to catch up.
Thank you so much.

171
00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:21.470
Laurie, his wife is here

172
00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:23.930
and I can't thank you enough for being here

173
00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:26.270
because hearing Kevin's story-
Neither can I.

174
00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:27.120
Neither can I.

175
00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:31.281
Thank you, thank you.
(crowd cheers)

176
00:06:31.281 --> 00:06:33.660
Victoria, you are a doctor.

177
00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:34.930
I am a doctor.

178
00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:39.433
And in that moment, what was it like for your perspective?

179
00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:42.110
Well, I was a brand new doctor.

180
00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:44.390
I was actually still a fourth year medical student,

181
00:06:44.390 --> 00:06:46.420
and then there was an emergency call

182
00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.510
to graduate all those fourth year medical students

183
00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:51.330
to increase the number of doctors that could work.

184
00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.930
And I had done all my training at that hospital.

185
00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.610
And I just figured in a time of mayhem,

186
00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:57.360 line:15%
this was a good way for me to give back

187
00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:59.290 line:15%
and take a little bit of control.

188
00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:02.510 line:15%
And I actually met Kevin after his critical illness

189
00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:05.230 line:15%
had already passed and I think that when you think of,

190
00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:07.250
you know, the ICUs and the intensity,

191
00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:09.270
obviously that part is very difficult to get through.

192
00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:11.070
But we also forget that

193
00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.140
once you've been in a bed for over 40 days,

194
00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:16.100
you got debilitated and there's a lot of work to do

195
00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.320
to get back to your normal baseline.

196
00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:21.360
And I just saw that he needed family, I, you know,

197
00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:22.520
family is what you need

198
00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.120
to get through these difficult things.

199
00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:25.930
How do you know to do things like that?

200
00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:27.710
Is there a person,

201
00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:28.950
a place, a thing,

202
00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:31.870
something in your life that catapults you

203
00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:33.920
to have that intuitive nature?

204
00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:36.350 line:15%
I just, that's what I was brought up doing,

205
00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.360 line:15%
was loving people and taking care of people

206
00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:40.440 line:15%
and treat everyone as if they're your own family.

207
00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.040 line:15%
And that's what I tried to do for you.

208
00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:44.813
Oh, thank God for people like you.

209
00:07:44.813 --> 00:07:46.563
(crowd applauds)

210
00:07:46.563 --> 00:07:49.384
Thank you, Dr. Victoria.

211
00:07:49.384 --> 00:07:50.830
And thank you, Kevin,

212
00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:52.680
for sharing your story

213
00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:56.560
and your family for being here and Dr. Victoria,

214
00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:57.980
I love your story.

215
00:07:57.980 --> 00:07:59.360
Thank you for sharing it with us.

216
00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:01.610
Thank you so, so much.

217
00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:03.885 line:15%
Thank you.
(crowd cheers)

218
00:08:03.885 --> 00:08:06.468 line:15%
(upbeat music)

